1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,352
听：A Brave Maid.

2
00:00:01,352 --> 00:00:02,705
跟读：A Brave Maid.

3
00:00:02,705 --> 00:00:23,079
听：A wooden vase from the Ming Dynasty at the entrance of the reception hall amazed everyone. The artists designed it in a rare style and selected valuable jewels to decorate it. People thought highly of its fancy colour of honey and the beautiful paintings on it.

4
00:00:23,079 --> 00:00:43,454
跟读：A wooden vase from the Ming Dynasty at the entrance of the reception hall amazed everyone. The artists designed it in a rare style and selected valuable jewels to decorate it. People thought highly of its fancy colour of honey and the beautiful paintings on it.

5
00:00:43,454 --> 00:00:57,503
听：The vase used to belong to a former castle. But when the country was at war, the enemy troops exploded the castle. Debates on how the vase survived went on and on.

6
00:00:57,503 --> 00:01:11,552
跟读：The vase used to belong to a former castle. But when the country was at war, the enemy troops exploded the castle. Debates on how the vase survived went on and on.

7
00:01:11,552 --> 00:01:35,758
听：In order to remove people’s doubt, a team of no less than 20 people carried out an informal investigation. The evidence they found showed that a maid took the vase apart and asked a sailor to sink it in a local well. She never gave away the secret even under the cruel trial of the enemies who were in search of treasures.

8
00:01:35,758 --> 00:01:59,964
跟读：In order to remove people’s doubt, a team of no less than 20 people carried out an informal investigation. The evidence they found showed that a maid took the vase apart and asked a sailor to sink it in a local well. She never gave away the secret even under the cruel trial of the enemies who were in search of treasures.

9
00:01:59,964 --> 00:02:04,256
听：It is worth giving this brave maid a fortune in return.

10
00:02:04,256 --> 00:02:08,548
跟读：It is worth giving this brave maid a fortune in return.
